        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I put a hot tub on my existing patio?",
            "answer": "<p>Sometimes, but only if the existing slab was poured thick enough and is still dead level. We'll check it for you honestly during the estimate rather than guess — a shell that sits on a twist is an expensive mistake.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does the pad need to be perfectly level?",
            "answer": "<p>Under the tub, yes — spa shells are designed to be fully supported and level. We slope the surrounding surface away for drainage while keeping the tub footprint itself true.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I can set the tub on it?",
            "answer": "<p>Concrete gains most of its strength in the first week. We'll give you a firm date at the pour so you can book delivery without guessing.</p>"
